REM ============================================================
REM  02 - LAUNCHING THINGS ON WINDOWS
REM  DuckyScript 1.0  ->  Pico Duck OK
REM
REM  Two ways to start a program:
REM    (a) Win+R then type the command  -> reliable, works on all versions
REM    (b) Win key then type the name   -> relies on Start Menu search
REM ============================================================

DEFAULT_DELAY 80

REM --- (a) Run dialog: calculator ---
GUI r
DELAY 700
STRING calc
ENTER
DELAY 1200
REM Close it again so the demo does not leave windows open.
ALT F4

REM --- (a) Run dialog: command prompt ---
GUI r
DELAY 700
STRING cmd
ENTER
DELAY 1200
STRINGLN echo DuckyScript can type into a shell too.
DELAY 400
REM "exit" is a command typed into the shell, not a key name.
STRING exit
ENTER
DELAY 500

REM --- useful single-key Windows shortcuts ---
REM GUI e   = File Explorer
REM GUI d   = show desktop
REM GUI l   = lock the workstation
REM GUI i   = Settings
REM GUI x   = the "power user" menu (same as right-clicking Start)
REM CTRL-SHIFT-ESC = Task Manager (no Win+R needed)

REM --- (b) Start Menu search ---
GUI
DELAY 600
STRING mspaint
ENTER
DELAY 1500
ALT F4

REM Gotcha: if Start Menu search is disabled or indexed badly,
REM method (b) silently fails on the first keystrokes. Prefer (a)
REM when reliability matters.
